\begin{abstract}
Training-free LLM information extraction degrades as schema complexity grows, yet prior work conflates two factors: type count and type confusability. We present what is, to our knowledge, the first controlled study isolating these factors across NER, RE, and event detection on four datasets, using the Schema Confusability Score (SCS) and its batch-level aggregation (BCS) as operational tools. Three findings emerge.
